==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Homura & Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Devil Homura''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Homura's main selling points are her above average range combined with overall fair stats. As is usually the case, [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] outperforms Homura in the realm of anti-Dark CC, so her Freeze shouldn't be viewed as anything more than an extra perk. Her attack power is good for how fast she attacks, and is useful in most situations. Her range is just enough to keep her out of immediate danger from common backliners such as [[THE SLOTH]] and [[Master A.]]

==='''True Form'''===
Devil Homura's role has shifted dramatically: from being a primarily crowd control based unit against Dark enemies, to a [[Long Distance]] [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]]/[[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] backliner with crowd-control capabilities. In many ways, she now functions as an entirely different unit.

While her standing range remains the same, her Long Distance is by far the most important change when discussing her True Form's performance. With a nearly non-existent blind spot, her LD should be viewed much like Omni Strike. This dramatically improves her matchups against midrange and backline enemies: including [[Professor A.]], [[Le'boin]] variants, and [[Fallen Bear]]. It doesn't restrict her usage against the notoriously aggressive Darks and Akus either. Furthermore, she's a rebound unit, so she can take advantage of enemies that repeatedly stagger her, and get successive attacks on them.

Devil Homura also receives [[Strong Against]], increasing her DPS to a solid ~9,300 vs. Dark and ~7,750 vs. Aku at Lv.30 (14,700 and 12,300 at Lv50). It also helps her shrug off some of the punishment that comes with that role (especially since Aku threats tend to abuse [[Death Surge]]s). However, it is important to note that she lacks any relevant Immunities, meaning enemies like [[Two Can]], [[Berserkory]], or even [[Sinner Snache]]s/[[Condemned Peng]]s can continuously pick her off relatively easily with their pierce, in a manner similar to [[Lilin (Uber Rare Cat)|Lilin]]. The absence of [[Shield Piercing]] further dulls her performance against Aku, requiring other suitable units to bypass them.

Her [[Freeze|Freeze]] should still be viewed as a bonus, as it is inconsistent at the best of times, and only reaches a 50% uptime with her extended attack cycle, if it activates at all. Fortunately, her long foreswing animation is not much of a problem due to the ludicrously high forward-pierce and inner-range of her Long Distance reach, she doesn't usually miss an attack.

Overall, Devil Homura is an incredible upgrade over her previous forms. Given the True Form's relatively low Catfruit cost and versatile performance, she is a valuable investment for any player looking for a unit that remains effective well into late-game.

